description:
The _generate_noise() function in background/paper_texture.py uses nested Python loops for upsampling:

for y in range(height):
    for x in range(width):
        noise_full[y, x] = noise_small[src_y, src_x]

For 1080p frames this is 2+ million Python loop iterations with array access. Should be vectorized using NumPy repeat/tile operations for 10-100x speedup.

This affects every frame generation, making it a significant bottleneck alongside text rendering.
